1 _OID 06975237-bd10-441b-ac32-2d11b003a8ba
1 _DSCR Hannah Feake, 1637-1678 , Massachusetts, Connecticut, New York, England  
2 CONT 
2 CONT The following is extracted from a very admirable paper prepared by the late John J. Latting and published in the New York Genealogical and Biographical Record, 1880. 
2 CONT 
2 CONT Hannah (2) (Feake) Bowne, b. supposed Watertown, Mass., about 1637; came with her mother and brothers and sisters to Flushing, L. I., about 1649; m. there 7/3 mo. (May) 1656, John Bowne, b. Matlock, Derbyshire, Eng., 9/3 mo. (May) 1627; d. Flushin
2 CONC g 20/10 mo. (Dec.) 1695. (See Bowne Lineage for issue)...and Hannah, the wife of John Bowne, having received a gift in the ministry made several religious visits to Friends in Great Britain, dying on the last one in England.
1 _META <metadataxml><cemetery /><transcription /></metadataxml>
