2 TITL Bears Genealogy p. 36
1 _OID 0bf80891-cd02-4df3-b7b9-a653690ba26e
1 _META <metadataxml><cemetery /><transcription>FOURTH GENERATION
2 CONT 
2 CONT this time to Thomas Annis of Barnstable, on Feburary 17, 1756.
2 CONT 
2 CONT 	Thomas and Lydia had a son, then Thomas diedl.  Widow Lydia came to Liverpool, Nova Scotia, brining her two sons and accompanied by her two brothers.  Lydia married her third husband Barnabass Freeman of Pleasant River.  Stepson Joseph Bearse Jr
2 CONC . was born around 1750, he was baptised on August 4, 1754.
2 CONT 
2 CONT 	"It is at this time that the name branched off from Bearce and Bearse to Barss." The name is recorded as Barss in the Liverpool records for this family.
2 CONT 
2 CONT _*_*_*_*_*_
2 CONT 
2 CONT *BENJAMIN BEARSE, Ben 3, Joseph 2, Augustine 1.
2 CONT 
2 CONT 	Born at Hyannis, Massl, on 26 March, 1710, son of Benjamin and Sarah (Cobb) Bearse. Ben married first wife Elizabeth daughter of Moses and Deborah (Cook) Godfrey on May 31, 1733.  Their children:
2 CONT 
2 CONT 	JOHATHAN [sic], born year 1734.
2 CONT 	MOSES, born year 1736.
2 CONT 	ELIZABETH, born in 1738.
2 CONT 	GEORGE, born year 1740.
2 CONT 	*BENJAMIN, born year 1742.
2 CONT 
2 CONT 	Elizabeth the mother died 1 December, 1742.  Benjamin re-married, this time in 1743 to Jane or Jean born at Chatham, Mass., year 1717, daughter of John and Hannah (Doane) Collins. At the date of her marriage to Ben she was the widow of Prince Sno
2 CONC w Jr. of Harwich, Mass., whom she had married at Harcourt, Mass., on 10 September, 1737.  Benjamin and Jean moved to Barnstable then to Harwich where Ben made the living for the family as a Blacksmith.  Their family:
2 CONT 
2 CONT 
2 CONT 36</transcription></metadataxml>
