1 _META <metadataxml><content><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: 'helvetica','sans-serif'; color: #1976d2; letter-spacing: .1pt;"&gt;Annapolis Spectator, Annapolis Royal, Oct 14, 1898&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</l
2 CONC ine><line>&lt;p style="margin-: 0in; margin-right: 0in; margin-bottom: 12.0pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'helvetica','sans-serif'; color: black; letter-spacing: .1pt;"&gt;Died - At Hillsburn, on Oct 9th, Mr. William Longmi
2 CONC re on Sunday night at age 96. Mr. Longmire was one of the pioneer settlers in this section of the country having lived here for over 50 years, where he raised a family of 10 children, two of whom are dead. The 8 children who survive him: Mrs W. Wil
2 CONC son, Mrs Benj. Halliday, Mrs Geo Halliday, Wm J. Longmire and Alfred Longmire of Hillsburn; Wallace Longmire of Milford, and Henry and Howard Longmire of Boston, Mass. He also leaves 51 grandchildren, and 72 great grandchildren. Mr Longmire worke
2 CONC d at shipbuilding in its palmy days. He was a wheelwright by trade. In his latter years he lived with his son Wm J.. His wife preceded him to the better land, nine years ago. He was a Baptist and the Reverend H. Achilles conducted the funeral. Hi
2 CONC s remains were interred at the Hillsburn cemetery by the side of his wife. One sister, Mrs James Withers of Granville Centre is the sole survivor of this long lived family.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="margin-: 0in; margin-right
2 CONC : 0in; margin-bottom: 12.0pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'helvetica','sans-serif'; color: black; letter-spacing: .1pt;"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 13.5pt; line-height: 115%; f
2 CONC ont-family: 'Helvetica','sans-serif'; color: #1976d2; letter-spacing: .1pt;"&gt;Weekly Monitor, Bridgetown, October 26, 1898&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</line><line>&lt;p style="margin-: 0in; margin-right: 0in; margin-bottom: 12.0pt;"&gt;&lt;span style=
